<title>GERMANY: Buba revises German March industry output upward.</title>
<headline>Buba revises German March industry output upward.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank provided the following revised index figures for German industry output:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT	Mar 97	   Feb 97</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)	 +0.3 (+0.5)    +1.8 (+2.0)</p>
<p> Year-on-year (pct)		   +3.8 (+4.7)    +6.6 (+7.0)</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		   100.5 (100.4)  100.2 (99.9)</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)	 +0.2 (0.1)     +0.8 (+1.1)</p>
<p> Year-on-year (pct)		   +2.6 (3.2)     +5.1 (+5.3)</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		    97.2 (97.0)    97.0 (96.9)</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)	 +2.8 (+6.8)   +10.3 (+8.8)</p>
<p> Year-on-year (pct)		  +11.7(+13.9)   +14.0(+13.4)</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		   143.6(145.3)   139.7(136.0)</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted. The percentage change figures are calculated by Reuters from the indices.</p>
<p>Previously announced data in brackets.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
